{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.PrintWriter;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class E3 {\n    public E3() {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        ArrayList<Integer> V = new ArrayList<>(), K = new ArrayList<>(), X = new ArrayList<>();\n        char[] s = sc.next().toCharArray();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (s[i] == 'V')\n                V.add(i);\n            else if (s[i] == 'K')\n                K.add(i);\n            else\n                X.add(i);\n        }\n        long[][][][] dp = new long[n + 1][n + 1][n + 1][2];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= n; i++)\n            for (int j = 0; j <= n; j++)\n                for (int k = 0; k <= n; k++)\n                    for (int d = 0; d < 2; d++)\n                        dp[i][j][k][d] = Integer.MAX_VALUE;\n        dp[0][0][0][0] = 0;\n        for (int v = 0; v <= V.size(); v++) {\n            for (int k = 0; k <= K.size(); k++) {\n                for (int x = 0; x <= X.size(); x++) {\n                    for (int t = 0; t < 2; t++) {\n                        long cur = dp[v][k][x][t];\n                        if (v < V.size()) {\n                            int vv = V.get(v);\n                            int m1 = rem(V, v, vv) + rem(K, k, vv) + rem(X, x, vv);\n                            dp[v + 1][k][x][1] = Math.min(dp[v + 1][k][x][1], cur + m1);\n                        }\n                        if (k < K.size() && t == 0) {\n                            int kk = K.get(k);\n                            int m2 = rem(V, v, kk) + rem(K, k, kk) + rem(X, x, kk);\n                            dp[v][k + 1][x][0] = Math.min(dp[v][k + 1][x][0], cur + m2);\n                        }\n                        if (x < X.size()) {\n                            int xx = X.get(x);\n                            int m3 = rem(V, v, xx) + rem(K, k, xx) + rem(X, x, xx);\n                            dp[v][k][x + 1][0] = Math.min(dp[v][k][x + 1][0], cur + m3);\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        long ret = Long.MAX_VALUE;\n        for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++)\n            ret = Math.min(ret, dp[V.size()][K.size()][X.size()][i]);\n        out.println(ret);\n        sc.close();\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    private int rem(ArrayList<Integer> arr, int ind, int val) {\n        int cnt = 0;\n        for (int i = ind; i < arr.size() && arr.get(i) < val; i++)\n            cnt++;\n        return cnt;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        new E3();\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    s = data[1].strip()\n    V = []\n    K = []\n    X = []\n    for i, ch in enumerate(s):\n        if ch == 'V':\n            V.append(i)\n        elif ch == 'K':\n            K.append(i)\n        else:\n            X.append(i)\n    v_size = len(V)\n    k_size = len(K)\n    x_size = len(X)\n    INF = 10**18\n    # dp[v][k][x][t] where t=0 last not V, t=1 last is V\n    dp = [[[[INF]*2 for _ in range(x_size+1)] for _ in range(k_size+1)] for _ in range(v_size+1)]\n    dp[0][0][0][0] = 0\n\n    def rem(arr, ind, val):\n        cnt = 0\n        for i in range(ind, len(arr)):\n            if arr[i] < val:\n                cnt += 1\n            else:\n                break  # since arr is sorted\n        return cnt\n\n    for v in range(v_size+1):\n        for k in range(k_size+1):\n            for x in range(x_size+1):\n                for t in range(2):\n                    cur = dp[v][k][x][t]\n                    if cur == INF:\n                        continue\n                    if v < v_size:\n                        vv = V[v]\n                        m1 = rem(V, v, vv) + rem(K, k, vv) + rem(X, x, vv)\n                        if cur + m1 < dp[v+1][k][x][1]:\n                            dp[v+1][k][x][1] = cur + m1\n                    if k < k_size and t == 0:\n                        kk = K[k]\n                        m2 = rem(V, v, kk) + rem(K, k, kk) + rem(X, x, kk)\n                        if cur + m2 < dp[v][k+1][x][0]:\n                            dp[v][k+1][x][0] = cur + m2\n                    if x < x_size:\n                        xx = X[x]\n                        m3 = rem(V, v, xx) + rem(K, k, xx) + rem(X, x, xx)\n                        if cur + m3 < dp[v][k][x+1][0]:\n                            dp[v][k][x+1][0] = cur + m3\n\n    ret = min(dp[v_size][k_size][x_size][0], dp[v_size][k_size][x_size][1])\n    print(ret)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.07287787614041e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.4543427823809907e-05, -3.421248038648628e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.005243359133601189, -0.00010251473577227443, -0